     "id": "comp-softmax-argmax-t1",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "MATHENE · matheme-softmax-argmax · DERIVED",
     "title": "Softmax and Argmax",
     "italic": "A retained distribution and an actual cut are different outputs.",
     "body": "p_i = exp(z_i/T)/Σexp(z_j/T): positive, summing to one; a common shift c leaves every probability unchanged — the invariance used for stability. z=(0,ln2,ln4) gives (1/7, 2/7, 4/7); T=2 flattens. T→0⁺: mass 1/k on the maxima — one-hot only when unique, else (1/2,1/2,0) against argmax's first-index rule; T→∞: uniform. Distribution, selection and draw are three different outputs; keep the field the cut travels with.",
     "x": 0.03,
     "y": 0.585,
     "width": 560,
     "size": 20,
     "align": "left"
    }
