     "id": "comp-preference-gauge-t1",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "MATHENE · matheme-preference-gauge · DERIVED",
     "title": "Preference Gauge and Reference Policy",
     "italic": "Differences can be fully legible while a shared numerical origin remains unidentified.",
     "body": "P(i≻j) = σ(r_i−r_j). Shifts r+c leave every comparison unchanged — the origin is unidentifiable from differences. (0,ln3): 3/4; shifted −20, still 3/4; scaled ×2, 9/10 — scale is not the invariance. DPO: β·log Z cancels between completions, leaving the log-ratio difference; changing the reference policy changes the comparison itself — 3/4 becomes 1/2. The neutral zero is already occupied; exposing that occupation can be part of the decision object.",
     "x": 0.03,
     "y": 0.585,
     "width": 560,
     "size": 19,
     "align": "left"
    }
